Templates support `if` and `loop` as final head suffixes.

If the head already contains a value, helper or directive, add a comma before
the control-flow suffix.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [if show:
        Visible
    ]

    [card, if show:
        Visible inside card
    ]
]

### Template `if`

A template `if` conditionally includes one body. Its selector is either a `Bool`
condition or an option-present capture. The captured value is scoped to the
body.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [if show:
        Visible
    ]

    [if maybe_name is |name|:
        Hello [name]
    ]
]

Runtime templates evaluate only the selected body. A false condition or absent
option produces structural no-output. Template control flow has no `else` or
`else if` form, and template loops have no `break` or `continue` controls.

For richer decisions in `.moth` code, choose a value with ordinary
value-producing `if` and then interpolate it:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    maybe_name String? = none
    name = if maybe_name is |present_name| then present_name else "guest"
    greeting = [: Hello, [name]]
]

This value-producing form belongs at supported receiving sites such as a
declaration; it is not an expression inside template interpolation. A `.mtf`
body remains const-required and cannot call runtime functions as a general
replacement.

### Template loops

Template loops repeat their body using the ordinary loop-header families:

- conditional loops
- collection loops
- numeric ranges

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [loop items |item, index|:
        [index]: [item]
    ]

    [loop 0 to 10 |value|:
        [value]
    ]
]

Collection and range loops may bind the current value and optional zero-based
index. Their source or bounds are evaluated once before iteration. Conditional
loop conditions are checked before each iteration. Iterations concatenate
directly without separators.

### Wrappers and no-output

A wrapper in the owning loop head wraps the complete aggregate once. Place a
per-iteration wrapper inside the loop body.

A false or absent conditional, a false conditional loop and a zero-iteration
collection or range loop produce structural no-output. Shared head wrappers and
parent `$children(...)` wrappers are skipped in those cases. A selected body
with no content is still selected, so its own head wrapper may render an empty
wrapper. A runtime expression that produces an empty `String` still produces
output.

### Fallible work and slots

Postfix `!` inside selected runtime template content propagates from the
enclosing function. Catch blocks are not template expressions. Runtime slot
applications remain valid inside a conditional body or loop body after normal
slot routing.

Compile-time template control flow, inactive-body validation and iteration
limits are specified by @../constants/#const-templates (Const templates).
